    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras face a challenging slate today, headlined by **Colt Keith**, who commands our highest efficiency score at 69.64. Benefitting from a favorable matchup against Grayson Rodriguez (xERA 4.95) and the prime #1 spot in the batting order, **Colt Keith** represents our most stable engine for counting stats. **Chase Meidroth** (66.48) similarly benefits from the soft matchup, leveraging a platoon edge to drive production from the leadoff position. While **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (63.34) faces a daunting assignment in Paul Skenes, his projected leadoff status, significant stolen base upside, and favorable wind conditions at the park provide enough of a floor to warrant an elite-level start, keeping him in the lineup despite the SP's dominance.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Pedro Ramirez**, who fell just shy of the threshold with a 38.14 score. While his switch-hitting versatility is an asset, the combination of a stagnant middle-of-the-order projection and the matchup against the elite Skenes made him the odd man out in favor of the higher-ceiling offensive opportunities presented by **Kazuma Okamoto** (62.30) and **Yordan Alvarez** (60.07). Owners should monitor the rain risk surrounding **Caleb Durbin** (41.87); while his speed is a critical component of our strategy, his matchup against Chris Sale is objectively unfavorable. If the weather in his game turns, we are prepared to pivot to maximize game caps and maintain our efficiency threshold. **Dillon Dingler** remains a functional start (53.61) against Rodriguez, though he remains a marginal play as we weigh his current consistency against the scarcity of SB contributors like **Trea Turner**, **Hyeseong Kim**, **Zac Veen**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Luke Raley**, **Josh Smith**, **Carson Benge**, **Casey Schmitt**, and **Luis Pena** currently held in reserve or roster depth.",
